## Next.js App Router (next-intl SSR)

- **File-based routing** - files in `app/` directory automatically become routes
- **Document routes live under `app/[locale]/*`** - next-intl SSR with `localePrefix: 'always'` (`i18n/routing.ts`); the next-intl middleware composed in `proxy.ts` redirects/rewrites unprefixed document requests to the locale-prefixed URL
- **Server Components by default** - all pages are Server Components unless marked with 'use client'
- **Non-document surfaces stay OUTSIDE `[locale]`**: `app/api/**` route handlers, `app/actions/` Server Actions, `app/sitemap.ts`, `app/robots.ts`, `app/dev/ui` (404 in production via `proxy.ts`)

## Route Structure (real map)

```
app/
  ├── layout.tsx                # Root layout: fonts, WebVitalsReporter, Providers,
  │                             #   title.default + title.template (NO Header/Footer here)
  ├── global-error.tsx          # Root catastrophic error UI
  ├── providers.tsx             # Client providers (analytics init on load/idle)
  ├── [locale]/
  │   ├── layout.tsx            # requireLocale → setRequestLocale → getMessages →
  │   │                         #   NextIntlClientProvider wraps Header / main / Footer
  │   ├── page.tsx              # Route: /en (home)
  │   ├── error.tsx             # Locale-scoped error boundary
  │   ├── not-found.tsx         # Locale-scoped 404
  │   └── example-form/
  │       └── page.tsx          # Route: /en/example-form
  ├── api/                      # Route handlers: health, vitals, csp-report, example-form
  ├── actions/                  # Server Actions (by domain)
  ├── dev/ui/                   # Dev playground (production returns 404)
  ├── sitemap.ts                # Dynamic sitemap with per-route hreflang entries
  └── robots.ts                 # robots.txt
```

No `loading.tsx` exists in the baseline — add one per segment only when a route
gains slow data fetching.

### Special Files

- **`layout.tsx`** - Shared layout for route segment and children
- **`error.tsx`** - Error UI (must be a Client Component); lives at `app/[locale]/error.tsx`
- **`global-error.tsx`** - Last-resort root error UI (`app/global-error.tsx`)
- **`not-found.tsx`** - 404 page (`app/[locale]/not-found.tsx`)
- **`route.ts`** - API route handler (`app/api/**`)

## Adding a Localized Route (danger zone)

Every `[locale]` page/layout entry MUST narrow the route param via
`requireLocale()` and call `setRequestLocale(locale)` **before any client
descendant renders** — a missing call swallows errors as `Error(void 0)` in
prerender (SKELETONS "i18n"). Mirror `app/[locale]/page.tsx`:

```typescript
// app/[locale]/blog/[id]/page.tsx
import { setRequestLocale } from 'next-intl/server';
import type { ReactElement } from 'react';

import { requireLocale } from '@/i18n/request-locale';

type Props = {
    params: Promise<{ locale: string; id: string }>;
};

const BlogPost = async ({ params }: Props): Promise<ReactElement> => {
    const { locale: rawLocale, id } = await params;
    const locale = requireLocale(rawLocale); // notFound() on unknown locale
    setRequestLocale(locale); // BEFORE any client descendant
    // ...
};

export default BlogPost;
```

- **Dynamic segments** work as usual, nested under the locale:
  `app/[locale]/blog/[id]/page.tsx` → `/en/blog/:id`; catch-all `[...slug]`,
  optional catch-all `[[...slug]]`
- **Params are async** in Next 16: `params: Promise<{ locale: string; ... }>` —
  always `await` them

## Metadata and SEO

- **Use `generateMetadata`** with `getTranslations({ locale, namespace })` for localized metadata
- **Every localized route builds `alternates.languages`** from `routing.locales`; `app/sitemap.ts` mirrors them as `<xhtml:link>` hreflang entries

```typescript
// app/[locale]/page.tsx
export const generateMetadata = async ({ params }: HomePageProps): Promise<Metadata> => {
    const { locale: rawLocale } = await params;
    const locale = requireLocale(rawLocale);
    const t = await getTranslations({ locale, namespace: 'meta.home' });
    const languages = Object.fromEntries(routing.locales.map((l) => [l, `/${l}`]));
    return {
        title: t('title'),
        description: t('description'),
        alternates: { canonical: `/${locale}`, languages }
    };
};
```

### title.template cascade (do not move)

`title.template` does **not** apply to the segment that defines it — only to
descendants. Root `app/layout.tsx` owns `title.default` + `title.template`;
`app/[locale]/layout.tsx` sets **only** `description` / `openGraph` / `twitter`.
Moving the template into `[locale]/layout.tsx` drops the brand suffix from page
titles.

## Layouts: root vs [locale]

| Layout                    | Responsibilities                                                                                                                                                                            |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `app/layout.tsx` (root)   | `<html>`/`<body>`, fonts, preconnects, `WebVitalsReporter`, `Providers`, `metadataBase`, `title.default` + `title.template`. **No Header/Footer, no i18n.**                                  |
| `app/[locale]/layout.tsx` | `generateStaticParams` from `routing.locales`, `requireLocale` + `setRequestLocale`, `getMessages` → `NextIntlClientProvider` wrapping `Header` / `main` / `Footer`; locale `description` / `openGraph` / `twitter`. |

The layout chrome (Header/Footer) MUST stay inside `NextIntlClientProvider` —
it consumes translations and breaks (hydration mismatch / prerender failure)
when rendered outside the provider boundary.

## Navigation (typed, locale-aware)

- **NEVER import `Link` from `next/link`, or `useRouter` / `redirect` / `usePathname` from `next/navigation`** for document routes — they bypass the locale prefix and produce un-prefixed (broken) URLs
- **Always import from `@/i18n/navigation`** (`createNavigation(routing)`): `Link`, `redirect`, `usePathname`, `useRouter`, `getPathname`
- **Exception**: `notFound` stays in `next/navigation` (no localized variant)

```typescript
// Client Component
'use client';

import type { ReactElement } from 'react';

import { Link, useRouter } from '@/i18n/navigation';

export const Navigation = (): ReactElement => {
    const router = useRouter();

    return (
        <nav>
            {/* renders /en/example-form */}
            <Link href="/example-form">Example form</Link>
            <button onClick={() => router.push('/')}>Home</button>
        </nav>
    );
};
```

## Route Organization Best Practices

- **New document route = new folder under `app/[locale]/`** — never at `app/` root
- **Route groups** `(group)/` still work under `[locale]` for organization without affecting URLs
- **Keep pages thin** - the RSC entry does locale narrowing + metadata; interactivity lives in a `*PageClient.tsx` client island (see `HomePageClient.tsx`)
- **Locale set stays `['en']`** until the caller explicitly asks to expand it (`i18n/routing.ts` + `messages/<locale>.json`)
- **Lazy load** heavy client components with `next/dynamic`
